<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yao Chang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">331–394</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yao Chang was a Qiang general who founded the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Serving the Former Qin, he rebelled after its defeat at the Fei River in 383, captured and killed the Former Qin ruler Fu Jian in 385, and proclaimed himself emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> in 386. He spent the rest of his reign fighting Former Qin remnants under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fu-deng">Fu Deng</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yao-chang.jpg" alt="Yao Chang" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see below · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harvard_drs_49802792_%E7%B9%A1%E5%83%8F%E4%B8%89%E5%9C%8B%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E7%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8_v.1_(%E5%A7%9A%E8%90%87).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
